<description>&lt;p&gt;The Colombian government has engaged U.S. intelligence and struck a deal with Venezuela to secure the release of two ELN hostages while President De la Espriella faces a surge of violence, including the killing of over 45 social leaders in his first 100 days. Petro has been accused of freezing the purchase of equipment to counter armed-group drones, and U.S. Secretary of War Pete Hegseth arrived in Bogotá to reinforce the security agenda. In Kyiv, a 19‑year-old woman was detained for poisoning a Colombian veteran of the Ukrainian Armed Forces for $1,000. Colombian land defenders continue to face lawfare and smear campaigns linked to a Canadian-owned copper project. The conflict recorded 225 battle-related deaths in 2024, according to UCDP.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Machine-written from the linked sources, checked for figures and names not in them.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;DW.com&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMilwFBVV95cUxNTmhGMS0yQS1vRVNiYUZWeUhQbTJScVNuRGIxZGRQN0xmbmxoelZHblE4RF80WVEwNDRVNmN6TEVXQ3diNzQ5Y3Mta0xmOGdmNFhwdDU3WHVmTmRjNmh3MEEzQVlBYVpSbjc2MWZudEtxc0VoeU92REh5TGItLUtpd3A1SDI4LTBfRVNTNWpJcVo3bnNITy0w?oc=5&quot;&gt;ColombiaOne.com&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiuwFBVV95cUxQdzJoRTVObUIwdGNHTkltOXNrcTZlYnVSUnR0T3pXRmZNNmZ2VENiQ2x5RFBZM3poUC1pSGRhNUZWck9zb1R6RjB4RXBzaEFOb3ZfMERHZUpVS012YzJhZVduVVJrRktERDc5anZrc1B3MU5Yby1UbVdqSHkzcHRuTWJZUHFqNTdqdEo3QWdXbUppeUtHQnQ3MndXS0VRbG1FMDFhU1EyRkVaWHFkNUFMT0drZm0wZHR2am9v?oc=5&quot;&gt;Washington Examiner&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMixwFBVV95cUxQNVBndk4yaU1yN3VCRzBsOXJfYWR2MnB2RnJ0MWJJZEJoU2ZvaVphYWJ4Mncwa0F3QV9wWkt4aVVKNlNucmxRaEJlVG9lbjVDaVA1MHZ3aHlYTnAwbWoxYW5XXzlRVkJQY0R6eFRtVUdxUlFTckZWMVJ5RnN1SmdZWnpiLURqdFNwZ1ZhU2ZLcXBRYVlVbzh1amVHZTg0X29iSDM4bWpYYXJmSlhMX3lRN1dMMjc1eHZLSGZHVEx2WGJDMmdfY2xz?oc=5&quot;&gt;Судово-юридична 